# 3. Assignment Operators

Used to assign or update variable values.

| Operator | Meaning               | Equivalent   |
| -------- | --------------------- | ------------ |
| `=`      | Assign                | `x = 5`      |
| `+=`     | Add & assign          | `x = x + 3`  |
| `-=`     | Subtract & assign     | `x = x - 2`  |
| `*=`     | Multiply & assign     | `x = x * 4`  |
| `/=`     | Divide & assign       | `x = x / 2`  |
| `//=`    | Floor divide & assign | `x = x // 3` |
| `%=`     | Modulus & assign      | `x = x % 2`  |
| `**=`    | Power & assign        | `x = x ** 3` |

Example:

```python
x = 10

x += 5     # 15
x *= 2     # 30
x -= 10    # 20

print(x)   # 20
```

Real-world uses include updating:

* Wallet/bank balances
* Bills
* Counters
* Scores

