# 4. Comparison Operators

Compare two values and return **`True` or `False`**.

| Operator | Meaning               |
| -------- | --------------------- |
| `==`     | Equal                 |
| `!=`     | Not equal             |
| `>`      | Greater than          |
| `<`      | Less than             |
| `>=`     | Greater than or equal |
| `<=`     | Less than or equal    |

```python
a = 100
b = 50

print(a > b)    # True
print(a == b)   # False
print(a != b)   # True
```

Example:

```python
age = 20
print(age >= 18)   # True
```

Useful for eligibility checks and validations.

