# 7. Membership Operators

Check whether an item exists inside a sequence such as a list, string, or tuple.

| Operator | Meaning             |
| -------- | ------------------- |
| `in`     | Item is present     |
| `not in` | Item is not present |

```python
ids = [101, 102, 103]

print(101 in ids)       # True
print(105 in ids)       # False
print(105 not in ids)   # True
```

Example:

```python
present = ["Raju", "Harish", "Ram"]

print("Raju" in present)
# True
```

Useful for searching lists, usernames, products, etc.

