# 10. Operator Precedence

When an expression contains multiple operators, Python follows a priority order.

### Highest → Lowest

```text
1.  ()
2.  **
3.  +x, -x, ~x
4.  *, /, //, %
5.  +, -
6.  <<, >>
7.  &
8.  ^
9.  |
10. ==, !=, <, >, <=, >=,
    is, is not, in, not in
11. not
12. and
13. or
14. Conditional expression
```

### Important

Parentheses `()` have the highest priority, so use them when you want to make the order clear.

